@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-use-structural-json-patch-diffs
+type: decision-log
+title: "Use structural JSON Patch diffs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients need compact RFC 6902 updates rather than complete replacement documents. Object changes can
+be represented directly at their JSON Pointer paths, while arrays also need to preserve inserts and
+removals.
+
+## Decision
+
+Generate recursive structural patches. Compare object members by key; compare equal-length arrays by
+index and use a longest common subsequence when their lengths differ, emitting only the needed array
+adds and removes. Use `replace` only when the values at a path cannot be decomposed further.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Small object changes and array insertions/removals remain small operations. Generation is deterministic
+and does not attempt RFC 6902 `move` detection, keeping patches straightforward and safe to apply.
